.Dd September 28, 2026
.Dt CFPREFSD 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm cfprefsd
.Nd per-user and per-system preferences daemon
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar daemon | agent
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the XPC service that backs the
.Xr defaults 1
command-line tool and the
.Li NSUserDefaults
machinery.
It owns all access to persistent property lists on behalf of its clients:
no client writes a preferences file itself, and the daemon serializes
concurrent access, resolves the search list that a given key is read from,
and posts change notifications to other clients.
.Pp
The daemon is not started by hand.
.Sy launchd
starts two instances of the same executable, distinguished by the single
argument each is given:
.Bl -tag -width "com.apple.cfprefsd.agent" -compact
.It Daemon
The system-wide instance, run as root, labelled
.Li com.apple.cfprefsd.xpc.daemon .
It exports the Mach service
.Li com.apple.cfprefsd.daemon ,
serves requests from any user on the system, and is the instance that
handles the Any User and By Host search-list domains, which must be
reachable by every session.
.It Agent
The per-user instance, run as the logged-in user, labelled
.Li com.apple.cfprefsd.xpc.agent .
It exports the Mach service
.Li com.apple.cfprefsd.agent ,
is registered in background sessions only, and serves that user's requests
so that preferences access remains available even when no Aqua session
is running.
.El
.Pp
The two roles have deliberately different Mach service names; a client
selects the daemon or the agent by which service it connects to, never by
which executable it runs.
.Pp
The executable itself contains no preferences logic.
It relabels itself through
.Xr libquarantine 3
so that the sandbox profile keyed to
.Li com.apple.cfprefsd
is applied to the process in place of one keyed to the image path, then
hands control to
.Fn __CFXPreferencesDaemon_main ,
which CoreFoundation exports.
The relabel covers the process itself, so a failure to apply it is fatal:
the daemon logs the failure and exits rather than running unconfined.
.Pp
If the quarantine relabel cannot be applied,
.Nm
logs a fault under subsystem
.Li com.apple.defaults ,
category
.Li cfprefsd ,
and exits with the status returned by
.Fn qtn_proc_apply_to_self .
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "~/Library/Preferences" -compact
.It Pa ~/Library/Preferences
Per-user search-list domains, one plist per bundle identifier and one per
host-qualified domain.
.It Pa ~/Library/Preferences/ByHost
Per-user By Host domains, keyed by host name.
.It Pa /Library/Preferences
The Any User search-list domain, written only by the daemon role.
.El
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
Failures in the quarantine relabel step are the only ones logged by
.Li cfprefsd
itself.
A client that cannot reach the expected Mach service is reported by
.Sy launchd ,
not by this program.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr defaults 1 ,
.Xr plutil 1 ,
.Xr libquarantine 3 ,
.Xr launchd.plist 5
.Sh HISTORY
This implementation is a clean-room rewrite of the CoreFoundation
.Nm
daemon, which is distributed in the base system but is not part of
Apple's published CoreFoundation source release.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An LibreDarwin
